1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,496
Day 53: CLI Agent Orchestrator,

2
00:00:02,496 --> 00:00:07,086
AWS's framework for coordinating multiple AI coding CLIs,

3
00:00:07,086 --> 00:00:10,066
tried with Claude Code as the worker.

4
00:00:10,516 --> 00:00:12,387
CAO runs a local server,

5
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:16,752
starts CLI agents such as Claude Code inside tmux panes,

6
00:00:16,752 --> 00:00:20,884
and lets a supervisor hand work off to those workers.

7
00:00:21,334 --> 00:00:24,767
A launch command tells the local server to create a session

8
00:00:24,767 --> 00:00:26,047
and a worker terminal.

9
00:00:26,497 --> 00:00:28,643
The server opens a tmux pane and

10
00:00:28,643 --> 00:00:30,855
types the claude command into it,

11
00:00:30,855 --> 00:00:34,543
with the flag that is meant to skip permission prompts.

12
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:38,775
This was Claude Code's first interactive run in the container,

13
00:00:38,775 --> 00:00:41,643
so it showed a theme picker, a security notice,

14
00:00:41,643 --> 00:00:44,571
and a folder-trust prompt instead of going idle.

15
00:00:45,021 --> 00:00:47,828
None of those screens cleared automatically,

16
00:00:47,828 --> 00:00:50,315
so the wait for an idle worker ran out.

17
00:00:50,765 --> 00:00:54,152
Every install and server-start step worked exactly as

18
00:00:54,152 --> 00:00:54,854
documented.

19
00:00:54,854 --> 00:00:57,730
Only the supervisor-to-worker handoff failed,

20
00:00:57,730 --> 00:01:00,541
with this exact timeout from the server log.

21
00:01:00,991 --> 00:01:04,810
Full write-up, including why we stopped instead of forcing the

22
00:01:04,810 --> 00:01:06,842
trust prompt through, is on Zenn.
